NAME
       grpck - check the group files for errors

SYNOPSIS
       grpck [-r] [-s] [group [gshadow]]

DESCRIPTION
       grpck reads /etc/group and /etc/gshadow and checks that every line has
       the right number of fields, that group names are valid and unique, that
       members are existing users and that each group in one file also appears
       in the other. It reports each problem it finds. When nothing is wrong it
       prints nothing and exits with status 0.

       Run it after editing the group files by hand (vigr is the safer way to
       edit them).

OPTIONS
       -r     Read-only: report problems but never offer to fix them.

       -s     Sort the entries of both files by group ID.

EXIT STATUS
       0 when the files are fine, 2 or more when problems were found or the
       files could not be read.

EXAMPLES
              # grpck -r && echo "group files look fine"

SEE ALSO
       group(5), gshadow(5), pwck(8), vigr(8), grpconv(8)
